==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission-matrix fact lets Alloy freely assign any (Role, OperationKind) pair to Allowed, immediately breaking LeastPrivilege (which requires specific denied cells) and PermissionCompleteness (which requires exactly 11 allowed cells).
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerPermissions, FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions, FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly, PermissionCompleteness
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that stops a single customer owning two in-flight applications. Injecting two in-flight applications for the same customer forces the FR-008 assertion to find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows a Decision's decidedBy field to reference a User other than the application's assignedOfficer. The injection forces a decided application whose decider differs from the assigned officer, violating FR-013.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides, AttributionCorrectness
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditInitialEvent  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditInitialEvent.als
    rationale: Removing the requirement for an initial audit event allows a LoanApplication to exist with zero ApplicationEvent entries. The injection creates an application with no events at all, directly violating AuditCompleteness.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_017_OneAuditEntryPerTransition, FR_022_RetentionNoDelete
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_OneAuditEntryPerTransition: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_022_RetentionNoDelete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing the uniqueness constraint on (application, prevStatus, newStatus) triples allows two event atoms to represent duplicate transitions — exactly what append-only forbids. The injection forces two events with the same application and same (prevStatus, newStatus) pair.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AssignedOfficerStatusConsistency  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AssignedOfficerStatusConsistency.als
    rationale: Clearing the status/officer coupling constraint allows a Submitted application to have an assignedOfficer, or an UnderReview application to have none. The injection creates a Submitted application with an assigned officer, violating the biconditional enforced by the data-model CHECK.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_AssignedOfficerStatusLink, FR_012_ExactlyOneOfficerPerApplication
      - FR_011_AssignedOfficerStatusLink: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_ExactlyOneOfficerPerApplication: PASS (vacuous?)

